    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey i keep getting this annoying SettingWithCopyWarning in my notebook when i try to add a new column to a dataframe i sliced earlier. like i did df2 = df[df['age'] > 30] then df2['status'] = 'adult' but it keeps throwing the warning. what is actually happening under the hood and how do i fix it properly?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "This warning occurs because pandas is unsure if you intend to modify a copy of the original DataFrame or the original DataFrame itself. When you slice with `df[df['age'] > 30]`, pandas might return a \"view\" or a \"copy,\" and assigning to it triggers the ambiguity warning. To fix this reliably, you should explicitly create a copy using `.copy()`: `df2 = df[df['age'] > 30].copy()`, and then you can safely add the new column.",
      "source": "target",
