    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense. i think i've seen people use .loc as well. is there a specific reason why .loc is preferred over just doing the slice and then the assignment? like is it fundamentally different in how it handles the memory?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Using `.loc[]` is preferred because it ensures you are explicitly selecting and setting values on the DataFrame in a single, unambiguous operation. While both methods can sometimes work, `.loc` prevents the fragmented view/copy issue by directly indexing and assigning data at the specified location. It gives pandas a clear instruction on precisely *where* to place the new data, which is much safer than relying on chained assignment after slicing.",
      "source": "target",
